"OverallSummary": "This case involves George Snyder IV, a former General Securities Representative with Ameriprise Financial Services, LLC, who willfully violated Regulation Best Interest (Reg BI) by recommending 33 purchases of leveraged exchange-traded funds (NT-ETPs) and crypto mining stocks to 18 retail customers without understanding the products or analyzing if they were in each customer's best interest. The Care Obligation violations occurred through the following failures: (1) Snyder lacked understanding of the features and risks associated with the investments, including the holding-period risk of NT-ETPs which are generally unsuitable for retail investors planning to hold them longer than a single trading session; (2) He conducted no research about the investments and didn't review prospectuses; (3) He failed to consider individual customer investment profiles, including varying investment objectives, risk tolerance, and age; (4) He recommended high-risk investments to customers with conservative or moderate risk tolerance, including 6 senior investors. Additionally, Snyder marked 32 order tickets as unsolicited when they were actually solicited, and exercised discretion without written authorization in 6 transactions. Customers suffered approximately $30,000 in realized losses, while Snyder earned $3,699.03 in commissions. FINRA imposed sanctions including a 5-month suspension, $10,000 fine, and disgorgement of commissions. The firm offered rescission to affected customers."
